# Exam track — Theme: Akafe Goen (Going Shopping) — Sub-lesson 1: Vocabulary
# Sproochentest oral-exam topic. Target level A1–A2 (authoring guideline only).
# The manifest id (shopping.01) is the authoritative identity; S1.01 is a label.
#
# Every sub-lesson mixes words AND sentences so each session alternates
# word-match and sentence-builder slots; the emphasis here is vocabulary.
#
# All @word LU sides verified with lod_lookup (lod.lu) for gloss + gender.

@lesson S1.01 "Shopping Vocabulary"

# --- Shops & places ---
@word den Akaf = the purchase
@word de Buttek = the shop
@word d'Geschäft = the store
@word de Supermarché = the supermarket
@word d'Epicerie = the grocer's
@word d'Bäckerei = the bakery
@word de Metzler = the butcher
@word d'Apdikt = the pharmacy
@word de Maart = the market
@word d'Keess = the till
@word d'Solden = the sales

# --- Money & paying ---
@word d'Geld = the money
@word de Su = the coin
@word de Präis = the price
@word d'Rechnung = the bill
@word de Bong = the voucher
@word d'Kaart = the card
@word de Portmonni = the wallet
@word de Wiessel = the change
@word d'Reduktioun = the discount
@word gratis = free of charge
@word bëlleg = cheap
@word deier = expensive

# --- Carrying & quantities ---
@word de Kuerf = the basket
@word d'Tut = the bag
@word de Sak = the sack
@word d'Lëscht = the list
@word d'Fläsch = the bottle
@word d'Stéck = the piece
@word de Kilo = the kilo
@word hallef = half
@word genuch = enough

# --- Food & goods ---
@word d'Iesswueren = the food
@word d'Wuer = the goods
@word d'Brout = the bread
@word d'Mëllech = the milk
@word de Kéis = the cheese
@word d'Fleesch = the meat
@word d'Uebst = the fruit
@word d'Geméis = the vegetables
@word den Apel = the apple
@word d'Gromper = the potato
@word d'Tomat = the tomato
@word den Zocker = the sugar
@word de Botter = the butter
@word d'Ee = the egg
@word d'Waasser = the water
@word de Kaffi = the coffee
@word d'Kleed = the dress
@word de Schong = the shoe
@word de Kaddo = the present
@word d'Gréisst = the size

# --- People ---
@word de Verkeefer = the salesperson
@word de Client = the customer

# --- Doing things ---
@word akafen = to do the shopping
@word kafen = to buy
@word bezuelen = to pay
@word kaschten = to cost
@word brauchen = to need
@word sichen = to look for
@word huelen = to take
@word kréien = to get
@word probéieren = to try on
@word frësch = fresh
@word zou = closed

@sentence
@lu Ech ginn all Samschdeg akafen.
@en I go shopping every Saturday.
@distractor-lu Sonndeg
@distractor-lu schaffen
@distractor-en Sunday
@distractor-en work

@sentence
@lu D'Brout an der Bäckerei ass frësch.
@en The bread in the bakery is fresh.
@distractor-lu Mëllech
@distractor-lu deier
@distractor-en milk
@distractor-en expensive

@sentence
@lu Ech bezuelen ëmmer mat der Kaart.
@en I always pay by card.
@distractor-lu Geld
@distractor-lu sichen
@distractor-en cash
@distractor-en look for
